   available only where `⟨y,y⟩ > 0`, so one argues with the **first zero** `z := sInf{t ∈ (0,t₁] :
   y t = 0}` (using `sInf_mem_of_isClosed_of_nonempty`): `z > 0` contradicts Sturm, so `z = 0`, hence
   `y` has zeros arbitrarily close to `0`, hence `y'(0) = 0` (mean value theorem along the sequence)
   and `y ≡ 0` by the linear second-order ODE uniqueness
   `Commons.Analysis.ODE.eqOn_of_secondOrder_linearODE` (massage the chart Jacobi equation into the
   `deriv(deriv y) = A t (y t) + B t (deriv y t)` form using `ChartCurv.hasDerivAt_chrB_curve` and
   the chart geodesic equation for `w`).
