With this the **upper Rauch comparison** (`sec ≥ K ⟹ ‖J(t)‖ ≤ sn_K(t)`, needed for Toponogov and
hence for Grove–Shiohama) is reduced to the following self-contained formalisation project
(`Submission/RauchUpper.lean`, not started):

1. **The coordinate curvature operator.**  For a unit-speed chart geodesic `(u,w)` on `(a,b)` and
   `t` in the interval put `Rop t := (v ↦ chartCurv cov x₀ ((extChartAt I x₀).symm (u t)) v (w t))`,
   a self-adjoint continuous endomorphism of `E` for the chart metric at the curve point.  Linearity
   is `Submission/JacobiVec.chartCurv_add_fst` / `chartCurv_smul_fst` (**available**); continuity is
   finite-dimensional; **self-adjointness for `chartGram` needs the first Bianchi identity**
