### 23.9 CORRECTION of an error in §23.8 of the previous handoff (IMPORTANT)

The previous handoff claimed that the critical missing comparison input was
"`sec ≥ 1` ⟹ no conjugate point before `π`".  **That implication is FALSE** (and so, of course, is
the plan built on it): a *lower* bound on the curvature makes conjugate points appear *earlier*
(a space form of curvature `4` has its first conjugate point at `π/2`), while an *upper* bound
`sec ≤ K` gives `conj ≥ π/√K`.  Concretely:

* `K_max ≤ 4` ⟹ `conj ≥ π/2` — **already proved** (`RauchGlobal.eqOn_zero_of_jacobi`,
  `ConjRadius.pi_half_le_of_isConjugateTime`);
* `K_min ≥ 1` gives the *upper* bound `‖J(t)‖ ≤ sin(t)‖J'(0)‖` (Rauch I, this session) — this is
  the input of **Toponogov's hinge theorem**, of the *concavity* of `d(p,·)` on `{d > π/2}`, and
  of the critical point theory of the distance function in Grove–Shiohama — it says nothing about
  the *existence* of conjugate points.

Consequently the correct interface for all the distance-function comparison arguments is
`Window` (`loewner_gen`, `rauch_upper_gen`), i.e. "on an interval without conjugate points", and
**no further local work is needed to reach `π`**: what is needed is the *globalisation* of the
window hypotheses along a geodesic (chart pieces + the transfer of the chart frames, as in
`GlobalBM`), and the `T < 2` restriction above is purely an artefact of the single-chart
`HasChartGeodesic` interface.

