### 26.2 The mathematical key

The chart Jacobi equation is `D(Dy) + R(y,w)w = 0`, i.e. `y' = u - Γ̂y`, `u' = -Γ̂u - R̂y`.  The
variation field `Y₀ = ∂_t (Φ(s,t)).1|₀` of a family of geodesics satisfies it because
* `Y₀' = Z₀` (Clairaut),
* `Z₀' = -dB(Y₀;w,w) - 2Γ̂(Z₀)` (differentiating the geodesic equation in `t`),
and the two combine into the Jacobi system **iff** the definition of `chartCurv`
(`dB(X;Y,Y) - dB(Y;Y,X) + chrB(chrB(Y,Y),X) - chrB(chrB(Y,X),Y)`) is rewritten with the slot
symmetries `dB_comm_snd`/`chrB_comm`, which is the content of `linearization_identity`.
Uniqueness of the linear ODE then forces `(Y₀, DY₀) = (D.Y · x, D.U · x)`.

