  exponential image of `-s • γ'(L)` (`hback`), one has for every `ε > 0` and all small `t > 0`
  `d(γ 0, exp_{γ L}(t • V)) ≤ ofReal (L + t * (⟨V, γ'(L)⟩ + ε))`;
* **`firstVariation_upper_geodCurve`** — the specialisation to the project's global geodesics
  `geodCurve (cov := cov) hmet T hT q ξ hξ`, with `hback` supplied by
  `GeoBack.geodCurve_sub_eq_expMap` and the smoothness/unit speed by `geodCurve_spec`.

Proof (the classical computation, with `δ = √t`): the backward point `γ (L-δ)` equals
`exp_{γ L}(-δ • γ'(L))` (`GeoBack`); the sub-arc `[0,L-δ]` is minimising
(`Minimising.riemannianEDist_eq_ofReal_of_unit_speed_of_minimising`); the chordal bound
(`ExpBound2.edist_expMap_le_chordal`, at the base point `γ L`) bounds
`d(γ (L-δ), exp_{γ L}(t • V))` by `ofReal √(chartGram (γ L) (γ L) (t•V + δ•wL) (…))`, whose
radicand is `t²A + 2 t δ B + δ² = t²A + 2t√t·B + t` with `A = ⟨V,V⟩`, `B = ⟨V,wL⟩`,
`wL = γ'(L)` (and `⟨wL,wL⟩ = 1`); the pure-numerical commons lemma
`Commons.Analysis.Calculus.eventually_sqrt_le_sqrt_add_mul_add` turns this into
`√t + t(B+ε)`; the triangle inequality and `L - √t + √t = L` finish.  All finitely many smallness
hypotheses are collected with a single `filter_upwards` (never with one `min` of all thresholds).

