Writing `chartGram z z a a = ⟪a, a⟫_{fibre at z}` (`chartGram_self_apply`), the ingredient is

> `∃λ>0, ∀z : M, ∀a : E, λ * ‖a‖² ≤ ‖(a : TangentSpace I z)‖²`   (**UCB**)

where the right-hand norm is the Riemannian (fibre) norm at `z` of the *identity* vector `a`
(recall `frameVector_self : frameVector z z a = a`, so the chart frame at the base point is the
identity).  `‖·‖` on the left is the fixed norm of the model space `E`.

### 34.3 WHY IT IS NOT IMMEDIATE

* `ChartBounds.exists_chartGram_bounds` gives (**UCB**) only *pointwise*: the constant depends on `z`.
