  `Continuous.inner_bundle` (Mathlib) the latter follows from the **continuity of the "constant
  section"** `z ↦ ⟨z, a⟩ : M → TangentBundle I M` — the section whose coordinates in the
  trivialization at `z` are constant.  In the general-bundle language this is
  `x ↦ TotalSpace.mk x ((trivializationAt F E x).symmL ℝ x a)`, i.e. the "identity identification"
  `F ≅ E x` (at the base point the trivialization is the identity).
* Mathlib's `eventually_norm_symmL_trivializationAt_lt`,
  `…_self_comp_lt`, `…_comp_self_lt` give local distortion bounds **but** with a constant built from
  `‖(trivializationAt F E x).linearMapAt ℝ x‖`, which for the tangent bundle equals the very ratio
  "model norm / fibre norm at `x`" that (UCB) is about — so the argument is circular with these
  lemmas alone.  `continuousOn_coordChange` is about *fixed* pairs of trivializations, so it does not
  see the varying base point of `trivializationAt`.

