### 41.4 GOTCHAS ADDED (continued)

8. **A radius returned by an `∃`-theorem cannot be related to its internal formula.**  Splitting
   `∃ ρ, 0 < ρ ∧ P ρ` via `obtain` makes `ρ` opaque; a later step needing
   `ρ ≤ √lam · (1/(2c))` (here: the phase-membership condition of `GExp_eq_chartFlow`) must get that
   bound *out of the theorem*.  `exists_uniform_chartFlow_comparison_ind` was therefore restated to
   take the chart bound `lam, hgram` as parameters and to conclude `ρ ≤ √lam·(1/(2c))` explicitly.
9. Statement shapes: a uniform comparison must be phrased with the *same* size hypothesis as its
   consumer (`r₁ + r₂ < ρ`, not `r₁ < ρ ∧ r₂ < ρ`), otherwise the dependent case (which needs
   `r₁ + r₂ ≤ π`) cannot be reached.
