### 44.6 ADDENDUM 2: CONCAVITY OF `d(p,·)` ALONG A FAR SEGMENT (`Submission/GSConcaveSeg.lean`)

NEW sorry-free file `Submission/GSConcaveSeg.lean` (ns `Submission.GSConcaveSeg`), imported by
`Submission.lean`.  Axioms: `propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound` only.

**`concaveOn_dist_geodCurve`** : if `γ = geodCurve hmet T hT q ξ hξ` is minimising on `[0,T]`
(`d(q, γ T) = T`), `t ↦ d(p, γ t)` is continuous on `[0,T]` with values in `[π/2, D]`, and
`T/2 + D ≤ π`, then `t ↦ d(p, γ t)` is **`ConcaveOn ℝ (Icc 0 T)`**.

Proof: for `x ≤ y` in `[0,T]` put `m = (x+y)/2`, `a = (y-x)/2`; then
`γ(m-a) = GExp (γ m) (a • ux)`, `γ(m+a) = GExp (γ m) (a • (-ux))` with `ux = -γ'(m)` (the ray
lemmas `GExp_neg_curveVelocity_geodCurve` / `GExp_add_curveVelocity_geodCurve`), all sides
minimising (`geodCurve_sub_arc_minimising'`), and Hopf–Rinow at `(γ m, p)` gives
`p = GExp (γ m) (r • up)` with `r = d(p, γ m) ∈ [π/2, D]`; the hypotheses `a + r ≤ T/2 + D ≤ π` and
`r ≥ π/2` make `GSConcave.edist_add_midpoint_le` applicable, giving
`d(p, γ(m-a)) + d(p, γ(m+a)) ≤ 2 d(p, γ m)`, i.e. the midpoint inequality.  Jensen's theorem
(`Commons.Analysis.Convex.concaveOn_Icc_of_midpoint`) then yields concavity.

This is the analytic core of **Grove–Shiohama step 2, case 2** in the range `diam ≤ 2π/3`: it turns
the pointwise concavity of `d(p,·)` outside the `π/2`-ball into the global chord inequality on the
segment `[x,q]` (of length `s ≤ D`, so `s/2 + D ≤ 3D/2 ≤ π`).  Combined with the fact that
`f(x) < f(q)` (from the uniqueness of the maximum, `step1_diameter_unique`) it gives
`(f∘γ)'(0⁺) ≥ (D - t)/s > 0`, hence `x` is not a critical point of `d(p,·)`.

