The argument (fully worked out, ~120 lines) is: suppose not; take `y n → x₀` violating points with
shortest directions `u n` and lengths `r' n`; write `u n = frameVector x₀ (y n) (w n)`; the chart
bound `lam ‖w‖² ≤ chartGram x₀ (y n) w w = 1` makes `(w n)` bounded, so a subsequence converges to
`w`; cut the geodesics at the fixed small time `t`; §47.2 gives `GExp (y n) (t • u n) → GExp x₀
(t • w)`; the two distance identities from `geodCurve_sub_arc_minimising'` pass to the limit; `d x₀
(GExp x₀ (t • w)) ≤ ofReal t` (`GExpRay.edist_GExp_smul_le_zero`) upgrades to equality by the
triangle inequality; §47.3 then shows `p = GExp x₀ (r • w)`, so `w` is a shortest direction at `x₀`
