* the chart-parallel section `y ↦ frameVector x y vv` is **continuous** on the chart piece at `x`
  (a `ContinuousAt`/`ContinuousOn` statement for the trivialization's `symmL`);
* a partition of unity on `M \ {p,q}` subordinate to the patches `U i` (Mathlib's
  `PartitionOfUnity.exists_isSubordinate` wants a *closed* set, so the cover has to be arranged to
  cover `univ`; the natural arrangement is to index by `M` and to add, for `i ∉ s`, an index whose
  patch is a small neighbourhood of `i` together with the *canonical* local field — the `U i` for
  `i ∉ s` must not meet `s`, which is why the naive `sᶜ` does not work: `sᶜ` is not open);
* hence `Σ i, ρ i x • W i x` is continuous: `PartitionOfUnity.IsSubordinate.continuous_finsum_smul`
