`w y = (e ⟨y, V y⟩).2`, which is continuous because `e` (a `PartialHomeomorph`) is continuous on its
source and `V` is a continuous section; summing the coordinates and applying
`continuousOn_symm` (or `continuousOn_symm_prodMk_left`, or `IsOpenPartialHomeomorph.continuousOn_symm`)
gives the result.  This is pure API plumbing, no new mathematics.

