This subsection records an analysis of the *merging* alternative of
`CutStep3.exists_two_minimising_or_not_locallyInjective` (the one hypothesis that is still missing:
`hloc_sphere`, i.e. `LocallyInjectiveAtGExp hmet p w` for `‖w‖ = m`).  Both a *positive* reduction
and the exact place where it fails are recorded, so that the next session does not have to redo it.

**Set-up.**  `InjAtLeast hmet p m`, `∀ r > m, ¬ InjAtLeast hmet p r`; the witnesses give
`Uₙ ≠ Vₙ`, `GExp Uₙ = GExp Vₙ =: yₙ`, `max ‖Uₙ‖ ‖Vₙ‖ < m + 1/(n+1)`, `Uₙ, Vₙ → u`,
