     `ContDiffAt.fderiv_right` + `clm_apply` for the velocity, the identification
     `deriv (fun x => Ψ (x,q.2)) q.1 = (fderiv ℝ Ψ (q.1,q.2)) (1,0)` being
     `Commons.Analysis.Calculus.deriv_slice_fst`.
4. `variationField_satisfies_jacobiSys_gen` with centre `c = t₀`, and then the **pair linkage**
   `gc Φ = ugeo`, `gv Φ = wgeo`, `Yp Φ = y`, `Ufun x₀ Φ = chartCovDeriv cov x₀ ugeo wgeo y`
   (the last one is the Clairaut identity `hasDerivAt_deriv_partial_swap` plus
   `chrB = christoffelEval ∘ frameVector` and `christoffelLM_apply`), giving the first-order system
   for the pair `(y, chartCovDeriv y)` at every `r` near `t₀`;
5. the eight `IsJacobiAt` conditions are then read off: (1)-(3) and (5) from the box and the
   `left_inv` of the chart, (4) from `curveVelocity_extChartAt_symm`,
