## 85. SESSION: **THE `inj ≤ ½ℓ` HALF OF CHEEGER–EBIN, OFF THE BROKEN LOOP** (`Submission/InjHalf.lean`)

### 85.1 The results

`Submission/InjHalf.lean` (new, imported by `Submission.lean`, sorry-free, `#print axioms` =
`propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound`):

* **`le_of_two_vectors_eq_GExp`** — the abstract form: two *distinct* tangent vectors `u ≠ v` at `S`
  with `‖u‖ = ‖v‖ = m` and `GExp S u = GExp S v` give `InjAtLeast hmet S r → r ≤ m`.  (These two
  rays form a closed loop of length `2m` through `S`; so the injectivity radius at `S` is at most
  half the loop's length.  Three lines from the definition of `InjAtLeast`.)
* **`GExp_eq_geodCurve`** — the `GExp`-ray *is* the canonical `geodCurve`: for unit `ξ` and `0 < m`,
  `GExp p (m • ξ) = (geodCurve … m hm.le p ξ hξ) m`.  Proved by geodesic **uniqueness**
  (`eqOn_Ioo_of_isGeodesicAt_of_eq`) applied to `t ↦ GExp p (t • ξ)` (smooth on all of `ℝ` by
  `LensLoop.contMDiffOn_GExp_smul`, geodesic everywhere by `GExpRayZero.isGeodesicAt_GExp_smul_all`,
  unit speed, initial velocity `ξ` by `GExpVelocity.curveVelocity_GExp_smul_zero`) and the canonical
  segment `geodCurve` (`geodCurve_spec`).  *This is the bridge that avoids the `unitOf`-dependent-rewrite
  trap entirely* (see 85.2 below).
* **`injAtLeast_le_corner_of_GExp_broken_loop`** — the same corner bound transported to the
  exponential-map form: from `GExp p (m•ξ) = GExp p (m•η)` (two unit directions `ξ ≠ η`, velocities at
  the corner distinct) conclude `InjAtLeast hmet (GExp p (m•ξ)) r → r ≤ m`.  This is the form the
  cut-point/Klingenberg ladder speaks.
* **`injAtLeast_le_corner_of_broken_loop`** — **the `inj ≤ ½ℓ` half at the corner of a broken
  minimising loop**: two unit-speed geodesic segments `G₁`, `G₂` of length `m` from `p` meeting again
  at `q` with a *genuine corner* (velocities at `q` distinct, i.e. not a back-and-forth traversal)
  satisfy `InjAtLeast hmet q r → r ≤ m`, i.e. the injectivity radius at the corner is at most half
  the length `2m` of the broken loop.  The two vectors at `q` are the **backward** rays
  `v_i = (-m) • Ġ_i(m)`, and the two continuation identities
  `GExp q ((-m) • Ġ_i(m)) = G_i 0 = p` are *verbatim*
  `HopfRinow2.GExp_neg_smul_curveVelocity_geodCurve` (backward ray continuation) with
