   velocity matching): the broken loop gives a closed *curve*; making it a genuine closed geodesic
   needs either a straight corner or the classical *shortening* (flushness) argument.  With §85 this
   and the odd-dimensional Morse-theoretic input of §80 are the only remaining gaps in the ladder up
