  no `haveI IsContinuousRiemannianBundle` is needed for this.)
* **`smul_left_cancel₀` does not exist** in this Mathlib revision.  To cancel `ε • _` use
  `congrArg (fun z => ε⁻¹ • z)` followed by
  `simpa only [smul_smul, inv_mul_cancel₀ hε.ne', one_smul]`.
* The **fibre norm is indexed by the base point**: `GExp q ((-ε) • ξ) = GExp q (ε • (-ξ))` is a
  `smul` identity but the two *terms* are not syntactically equal, and `‖ε • v₁‖` and `‖(-ε) • v₁‖`
  are different hypotheses.  Keep both (`hnorm1`, `hnorm1'`).
* **The `set`-based base-point discipline.**  To avoid the dependent-rewrite trap of §84.4, make the
  base point of every tangent vector *syntactically* the same expression: `set w : TangentSpace I
  (GExp q ((-ε) • ξ)) := curveVelocity … with hwdef` and *never* name the point itself with `set`
  (naming the point makes `TangentSpace I A` and `TangentSpace I (GExp q ((-ε)•ξ))` different
  types).  All the `hAw`/`hA2w`/injectivity steps of §87.2 then go through with no transport at all.
* `curveVelocity_comp_mul_add` (the translation chain rule) is the only tool for the velocity of a
  translated curve; write the curve in the form `fun s => γ (c * s + d)` so that `rw` matches, and
