* A `by simp only [zero_smul, GExp_zero, one_mul, zero_add]` closes a value-equality between two
  *lambdas applied at a point* cleanly (it beta-reduces); `show`-based statements of the same thing
  need the whole vector term spelled out.
* **`match` does not reduce at a stuck index.**  With `piece : ℕ → ℝ → M := fun i => match i with
  | 0 => … | 1 => … | _ => …`, the goal `ContMDiff … (piece (0 + 1))` does not unfold; `rcases i with
  _ | _ | i` gives the cases `0`, `0 + 1` and `i + 2`, and only the `show` with the *explicit*
