## 95. SESSION: **THE CHART DATA OF A `GExp`-RAY IN A PRESCRIBED CHART**
(`Submission/GeoChartCurve.lean`)

Two new imported, sorry-free, axiom-clean modules this session: `Submission/SingularConj.lean` (§94)
and `Submission/GeoChartCurve.lean` (§95).  Everything below is namespace
`Submission.GeoChartCurve`.

### 95.1 Why a *prescribed* chart

The whole local/analytic machinery of the project (`Submission/RayChart.exists_pos_chartODE_GExp`,
`Submission.GeodesicGlobal.chartODE_of_isGeodesic`, `ChartPieces.exists_chart_pieces`, `GlobalBM`)
produces the chart geodesic equation in the chart **`chartAt H (γ t)` centred at the current point of
the curve**.  `Submission.IndexCorner2.eqOn_zero_of_minimising_chart`, in contrast, needs the chart
data of a `GExp`-ray in **one prescribed chart `x₀`** on a whole interval.  The bridge is the
**chart-independence of the geodesic equation**, which the project already has:

> **`Submission.GeodesicExtend.hasDerivAt_deriv_chartCurve_of_isGeodesicAt`** — if `γ` is an intrinsic
> geodesic at `t₀` with nonzero velocity, smooth near `t₀`, and `γ t₀ ∈ (chartAt H x₀).source`, then
> `HasDerivAt (deriv (fun t ↦ (extChartAt I x₀) (γ t)))
>   (chartGeodesicVectorField cov x₀ ((extChartAt I x₀) (γ t₀), deriv (… ) t₀)) t₀`.

### 95.2 What was proved

* `hasDerivAt_chartCurve_GExp` — the coordinate curve `t ↦ (extChartAt I x₀) (GExp p (t • ξ))` of a
  `GExp`-ray (`ξ ≠ 0`) is differentiable at `s`, for `s` in the chart;
* `hasDerivAt_deriv_chartCurve_GExp` — its velocity again has derivative the **chart geodesic spray**
  `chartGeodesicVectorField cov x₀ (u, w)` (immediate from `hasDerivAt_deriv_chartCurve_of_isGeodesicAt`
  + `LensLoop.contMDiffOn_GExp_smul` + `GExpRayZero.isGeodesicAt_GExp_smul_all` +
  `RayChart.curveVelocity_GExp_ne_zero`);
* `chartGeodesicEquation_GExp` — the same in the form `w' + chrB cov x₀ γ w w = 0` that
  `IndexCorner2` consumes (`chartGeodesicVectorField = -chrB` by definition, so this is `abel`);
* `chartGram_chartCurve_GExp` — **unit speed in the chart**: for `‖ξ‖ = 1` the chart Gram form of the
  coordinate velocity is `1`.  Proof: the chain rule
  `GlobalBM.deriv_extChartAt_eq_continuousLinearMapAt_curveVelocity`, then
  `GlobalBM.chartGram_continuousLinearMapAt` (which turns the chart Gram form into the *fibre* inner
  product `⟪γ̇, γ̇⟫`) and `real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq`, then `‖γ̇(s)‖ = ‖ξ‖ = 1` from
  `LensLoop.norm_curveVelocity_GExp_smul_ne` (with the degenerate case `s = 0` handled by
  `GExpVelocity.curveVelocity_GExp_smul_zero`);
* **`chartGeodesicData_GExp`** — the package: for a unit `ξ` and a chart `x₀` containing
  `GExp p (s • ξ)` for all `s ∈ Icc (-1) (L+1)`, all five geodesic facts of
  `IndexCorner2.eqOn_zero_of_minimising_chart` hold on `Icc (-1) (L+1)` (differentiability, the spray
  equation, target membership, the `chrB` form, and unit speed);
* **`hasChartGeodesicOn_GExp`** — the same data in the **bundled** form
  `Submission.RauchGen.HasChartGeodesicOn`, which is what
  `Submission.ChartGeoAt.exists_jacobiSystemOn` (the Jacobi tensor along a chart geodesic) consumes.
  Since that bundle initialises at parameter `0`, the ray is re-parametrised:
  `u s = (extChartAt I x₀) (GExp p ((t₀+s) • ξ))`, `w s = deriv u s`, `q = GExp p (t₀•ξ)`,
  `v = curveVelocity (ray) t₀`.  The translation is handled by
  `Submission.GlobalBM.hasDerivAt_comp_const_add`, and the initial velocity by
  `Length.curveVelocity_comp_mul_add` + `GeodesicExtend.curveVelocity_congr_of_eventuallyEq`.
  **Gotcha**: `GlobalBM.hasDerivAt_comp_const_add`'s conclusion has `f (c+s)`; `rw` will *not* descend
  under the binder of the resulting lambda, so a later `rw [h]` for the *function* must be replaced by
  `HasDerivAt.congr_of_eventuallyEq` with an eventual equality on a neighbourhood of the point (here
  `isOpen_Ioo.mem_nhds hs`); the *derivative* argument can be rewritten by `rw` after a `show` that
  beta-reduces the `(fun s ↦ w s) s` redex in `HasChartGeodesicOn`'s clauses.

### 95.2b `Submission/RayJacobiTensor.lean` — the Jacobi system along a `GExp`-ray

New imported module (namespace `Submission.RayJT`), one theorem:

> **`exists_jacobiSystem_GExp`** — for a unit... (indeed any non-zero) `ξ`, `0 < L`, and a prescribed
> chart `x₀` containing the ray on `Icc (-1) (L+1)`, there are `Y U : ℝ → E →L[ℝ] E` with `Y 0 = 0`,
> `U 0 = 1` and, on `Icc 0 L`,
> `Y' = U - Γ̂ ∘ Y`, `U' = -Γ̂ ∘ U - R̂ ∘ Y`, where `Γ̂`, `R̂` are the Christoffel and curvature
> operators along the chart image `u s = (extChartAt I x₀) (GExp p (s • ξ))`, `w = u'`.

Proof: `ChartGeoAt.exists_jacobiSystemOn` fed with the `HasChartGeodesicOn` bundle of §95.2.  The only
bookkeeping is that the bundle is paramerised by `(0 + s)` (its `u` is
`fun s ↦ (extChartAt I x₀) (GExp p ((0 + s) • ξ))`), so one rewrites with
`hu : (fun s ↦ … ((0 + s) • ξ)) = (fun s ↦ … (s • ξ))` (by `funext` + `zero_add`).  **Gotcha**: this
single `rw [hu] at h` also rewrites the velocity `w` occurring *inside* `Γ̂`/`R̂` (it is
`fun s ↦ deriv (fun r ↦ … ((0 + r) • ξ)) s`, and `hu` rewrites the inner function), so no second
rewrite is needed — attempting one fails with "pattern not found".

### 95.2c `Submission/RayJacobiTensor.lean` (continued) — the columns are Jacobi fields

Two more declarations (after the `abbrev`s `rayU`, `rayW` for the chart image and chart velocity of the
ray — **`abbrev`, not `def`**, so that `simpa`/`exact` see through them by defeq; a plain `def` is *not*
unfolded by `simp only [rayU]` in these goals):

> **`isJacobiAt_rayCol`** — for a unit `ξ`, a chart `x₀` containing the ray on `Icc (-1) (L+1)`, and a
> Jacobi system `(Y, U)` along the ray with the two ODEs on `Ioo (-1) (L+1)`, the column
> `s ↦ frameVector x₀ (GExp p (s • ξ)) (Y s a)` **is a Jacobi field in the sense of
> `RauchGlobal.IsJacobiAt`** at every `s₀ ∈ Icc 0 L`.

All eight germ clauses are assembled from existing lemmas: target membership from the chart data;
`HasDerivAt rayU rayW` from `GeoChartCurve.hasDerivAt_chartCurve_GExp`; `γ = (extChartAt)⁻¹ ∘ rayU`
from `PartialEquiv.left_inv`; the frame identity is `rfl`; unit speed from
`GeoChartCurve.chartGram_chartCurve_GExp`; the two differentiability clauses from
`JacobiTensor.hasDerivAt_jacobiCol` and `RauchGen.JData.hasDerivAt_chartCovDeriv_jacobiCol_Ioo`
(each closed with `rw [h.deriv]`); and the Jacobi equation from
`RauchGen.JData.jacobiEquation_col_Ioo` (its source-membership hypothesis is
`ChartConnection.mem_source_chartCurve` applied to `(extChartAt I x₀).map_source …` — note that
`mem_source_chartCurve` takes a **target** membership as input and *produces* the source membership,
so the argument is a `map_source`, not a `extChartAt_source` rewrite of `hsrc`).

Consequence: any vanishing of a column at a positive time gives a `ConjRadius.IsConjugateTime`, so the
Jacobi tensor is now accessible to the whole `IsJacobiAt`-based theory of the library.

### 95.3 The precise remaining gap for the intrinsic `σ ≤ κ` (important)

`IndexCorner2.eqOn_zero_of_minimising_chart` also needs the **Jacobi** field `J` in chart `x₀`
coordinates: functions `J, J' , J'' : ℝ → E` with the two `HasDerivAt`s, `frameVector x₀ (γ t) (J t) = Jfield t`,
and the chart Jacobi equation `DtDsP cov x₀ u J w J' t + chartCurv (γ t) (J t) (w t) = 0`.

The library's notion of "`J` is a Jacobi field along `γ`" is `RauchGlobal.IsJacobiAt`, which is an
**existential over charts**: *some* chart carries the equation near `t`.  What was missing is the
analogue of `§95.1` for Jacobi fields:

> ~~**MISSING (`chart-independence of the Jacobi equation`).**~~  **DONE** — see §95.7.
> `Submission.ChartIndep.chartJacobiEquation_of_charts`: the chart Jacobi equation, read through the
> *same* global sections of the tangent bundle, holds in one chart containing the curve iff it holds
> in any other.  The proof does **not** use the transformation law of Christoffel symbols (Route 1) or
> the variation-field route (Route 2) below: it uses the **intrinsic formula for `∇` of a global
> smooth section** `cov_eq_frameVector_coordFun`, which converts the chart expression for the
> covariant derivative along a curve into the chart-free `cov W (γ t₀) (curveVelocity γ t₀)` (and
> `curvVec_frameVector_eq`, which does the same for the curvature term).  The remaining assembly for
> `IsJacobiAt ⟹` chart-`x₀` equation is the *production* of the two global sections from the
> `IsJacobiAt` data (§95.7).

### 95.4 A second, cheaper observation: the Jacobi *tensor* route

`IndexCorner2`'s argument only needs *some* non-trivial Jacobi field vanishing at `0` and `t₀`.  The
field `s ↦ frameVector x₀ (γ s) ((Y s) x)` — the `x`-column of the **Jacobi tensor** `Y` of the ray
in the chart `x₀`, produced by `ChartGeoAt.exists_jacobiSystemOn` from the chart geodesic data of
