tensor is reachable without §95.3**:

> **Candidate.**  `sec`-free: for a unit `ξ`, a chart `x₀` containing the ray on `[0,L]`, `hmin`,
> and `x ≠ 0`, `(Y t) x ≠ 0` for all `t ∈ (0,L)` — where `Y` is the chart-`x₀` Jacobi tensor along the
> ray.

Consequences: `Y t` is invertible on `(0,L)` (a "no conjugate point" statement in the tensor form),
and `IsJacobiAt` for the columns follows by direct construction, so this *does* give
