### 96.4 Why the global `σ ≤ κ` is still open — the localisation attempt, and its exact failure

The natural hope after §96.3 is to *localise*: the corner argument of `IndexCorner2` uses a
perturbation `W` supported in a small chart neighbourhood of the corner, so maybe the whole proof can
be run with one chart near the conjugate time, avoiding the "one chart for the whole minimising
segment" hypothesis of `eqOn_zero_of_minimising_chart`.  **This fails**, and the reason is worth
recording precisely.

Let `γ` be minimising on `[0,T]`, `J` a Jacobi field with `J(0) = J(t₀) = 0` (`t₀ < T`), and consider
the localised variation supported in `[t₀-δ, t₀+δ]` with field `J + εW` on `[t₀-δ,t₀]` and `εW`
after.  Its second energy variation is
`E''(0) = -2[A + 2ε⟨∇J(t₀), W(t₀)⟩ + ε²(C₁+C₂)]` with `A = ⟨∇J(t₀-δ), J(t₀-δ)⟩`, the **boundary term
at the left end of the localised piece**.  In the original (global) argument `A = 0` *because
`J(0) = 0`*; in the localised version `A` is an arbitrary real number, and the quadratic in `λ`
(where `W(t₀) = -λ∇J(t₀)`) has minimum `-2A - 2c²/C` (with `c = |∇J(t₀)|²`, `C = I(W₀,W₀)`), which is
**not** necessarily negative.  So the localisation loses exactly the information that makes the
argument work.  This is the precise sense in which (as §92.3/§92.4 already said) "only the global
broken-Jacobi-field construction shortens".

**Consequence (the honest plan).**  The global `σ ≤ κ` needs an **intrinsic index form**: the integral
`∫_0^{t₀} (⟨∇J,∇J⟩ - ⟨R(J,γ')γ',J⟩) dt` of a Jacobi field over an interval that *crosses charts*,
together with
* (i) additivity over a chart decomposition of `[0,t₀]` (each piece contributes
  `⟨∇J(b),J(b)⟩ - ⟨∇J(a),J(a)⟩`, so the sum telescopes to zero when `J(0) = J(t₀) = 0`);
* (ii) the *global* second variation of the energy for a variation whose field is a broken Jacobi
  field plus a localised perturbation;
* (iii) the index lemma `I(V,V) ≤ 0` for a field vanishing at the ends of a sub-segment of a
  minimising geodesic (`Submission/IndexLemma.indexIntegral_nonpos_of_minimizing`), which is what
  replaces the unavailability of `I(V,V) = 0` in the localised setting.

The intrinsic quantities exist: the fibre inner product is global, `⟪∇J, W⟫` is computed
chart-freely by `ChartCurv.cov_eq_frameVector_coordFun`, and the curvature term by
`curvVec_frameVector_eq`.  What must be built is the *packaging*: a chart-independent integrand
`t ↦ ⟨Z t, Z t⟩ - ⟨curvVec(W t, vel t) vel t, W t⟩` for a field along `γ` together with its covariant
derivative, its agreement with `indexIntegrand` on each chart piece, and the additivity of its
integral.

