### 96.6 Gotchas found this session (they cost real time)

* **`set x : T := e with hx` followed by `simpa only [hx]` can fail on *defeq* function forms.**
  `(fun s => f s) - g` and `fun s => f s - g s` are related by `rfl` under `funext`, but `exact`/`simpa`
  as produced by `HasDerivAt.sub` / `ContinuousOn.sub` will not accept the other form.  The reliable
  pattern is: `have hh : (fun s => f s) - g = fun s => f s - g s := by funext s; rfl`, then
  `rw [hh] at h`, then put the goal into the same shape with `rw [hdef]` and `exact h`.
* **Rewriting a `set`-introduced function inside an applied position produces a beta-redex** that a
  later `rw [hdef]` cannot see: use `simp only [hdef, ...]` (simp beta-reduces) instead of `rw [...]`.
* **`HasDerivAt.congr_of_eventuallyEq` wants `h' : g =ᶠ f` with the *goal* being `HasDerivAt g`** (the
  reverse of the `ContinuousOn.congr` convention, which wants `EqOn g f s` with goal `ContinuousOn g`).
* **`Icc_mem_nhds h₁ h₂` needs *strict* bounds**, so it cannot be used at the endpoints of the interval
  that the hypotheses are stated on; this is why the hypotheses live on `Icc (-1) (L+1)` while all the
  internal lemmas live on `Ioo (-1) (L+1)`.
* **`E × E × E` parses as `(E × E) × E`**; `(fun p : E × (E × E) => p.2.1)` and `p.2.2.2` are the
  projections one wants (recall §95.8).
* **Named implicit arguments must precede all positional ones**: to apply
  `eqOn_zero_of_minimising_chart` with its implicit `{J J' J'' t₀}` one must write
  `... (J := J) (J' := J') (J'' := J'') (t₀ := t₁) hmet htor x₀ hL …`, and the *explicit* `ht₀`, `htL`
  arguments must still be supplied (they are not inferred from the goal).
* `GExp` (and hence `RayJT.rayU`, `rayJT.rayW`) carries `[Nontrivial E] [CompactSpace M]` as instance
  arguments; a statement mentioning `GExp` silently acquires them.
* `rw [chartGeodesicVectorField, ...]` fails ("Failed to rewrite using equation theorems"): use
  `simp only [chartGeodesicVectorField, chrB_apply]` and then `abel`.


