## 100.4 The phase condition for `|σ| ≤ 1` (why it is there, and why it is harmless)

`psiV_zero` is proved from `UniformInj.hasDerivAt_Hfun_along`, which needs the phase
`(x t, flowScale D • u t) ∈ D.O` — i.e. the phase condition **at `σ = 1`**.  The theorem
`energy_second_deriv_fam` only needs the phase for `|σ| ≤ δ`, so `energy_second_deriv_piece` takes
`δ := 1` and demands the phase for `|σ| ≤ 1`.  This costs nothing in the application: for a field of
size `λ` the phase condition at `σ = 1` holds whenever `flowScale D * ‖u‖ ≤ 1`, i.e. after
**rescaling the field** (`u ↦ u/λ`, which multiplies `E''(0)` by `λ²` and the integral of `idxAlong`
by `1/λ²` — the factors cancel), see §100.5.

