   `IsConjugateTime` we get an intrinsic field `J` with `IsJacobiAt cov γ J s` for **every** `s`.
   Per point `s ∈ [0,t]`, `RauchGlobal.exists_local_data` gives a chart `x`, coordinate functions
   `u, w, y` and a radius `ρ > 0` with the *local* data of `J` on `Ioo (s-ρ) (s+ρ)`; a finite
   subcover of `[0,t]` plus `Commons.Topology.Order.exists_partition_subordinate_Icc` gives a
   partition with per-piece `IsJacobiPiece`/`IsBilPiece` data (item 2 of §100.5 uses only the
   `Icc A B` hypotheses, which this provides).
2. **The regularity bridge (the only real gap).**  `IsJacobiAt`'s data is only `C¹`-level
   (`HasDerivAt u w`, `HasDerivAt y (deriv y)`), while `energy_second_deriv_piece` wants
   `ContDiffOn ℝ ∞` of the coordinate curves.  The bridge is the **Jacobi system**: with
   `z := chartCovDeriv cov x u w y` the `IsJacobiAt` equations read
   `deriv y = z - Γ(w, y)`, `deriv z = -Γ(w, z) - R(y, w)w`
   (the second one is `chartCovDeriv (chartCovDeriv y) + chartCurv y w = 0` unfolded; the *definitional*
   identification `chartCovDeriv Y = deriv Y + Γ(w,Y)` is what makes it work), and
   `CoeffSmooth2.contDiffOn_of_jacobiSolution` turns any solution of that linear system on `Icc a b`
   into `C^∞` data.  (`IndexMin.DtDsP_eq_chartCovDeriv_chartCovDeriv` is the existing bridge between
   the `DtDsP` and the `chartCovDeriv` formulations.)
3. **The perturbation.**  `V_ε := J + ε W` with `J` extended by `0` past `t` and `W` a bump supported
   near `t` with `W t = -∇J(t)` (`∇J(t) ≠ 0` because a nonzero Jacobi field vanishing at `0` and `t`
   has nonzero covariant derivative there — `IndexCorner2.eqOn_zero_of_chartJacobi`).  The family
   `Φ_σ(s) = GExp (γ s) (σ • V_ε s)` has fixed endpoints (`V_ε 0 = V_ε L = 0`) and `V_ε` vanishes at
   the partition points, so each piece's field *is* cut off there — the per-piece hypotheses of
   `energy_second_deriv_piece` hold with `u a = u b = 0` on every piece.
4. **The evaluation of `E''(0).`**  `E''(0) = 2 ∫_0^t idxAlong(V_ε, ∇V_ε)` (the assembly, item 2 of
   §100.5) `= 2[∫ idxAlong(J,∇J) + 2ε∫ bilAlong(J,W,∇J,∇W) + ε²∫ idxAlong(W,∇W)]`
   `= 2[0 + 2ε⟪∇J(t),W(t)⟫ + ε²C]` using the **already available cover lemmas**
   `IndexIntrinsic2.integral_idxAlong_eq_zero_of_cover` and
   `IndexIntrinsic2.integral_bilAlong_corner_of_cover`; with `W(t) = -∇J(t)` this is
   `-4ε‖∇J(t)‖² + 2ε²C < 0` for small `ε > 0` (commons lemma
   `Commons.Analysis.Calculus.exists_pos_four_mul_sub_sq_mul_neg`).
5. **The contradiction.**  `E(σ) ≥ L` for all `σ` (`EnergyBound.le_energy_of_edist_eq`, endpoints
