* pointwise: `IndexIntrinsic2.hasDerivAt_inner_idxAlong` (resp. `hasDerivAt_inner_bilAlong`) gives
  `HasDerivAt (fun s => ⟪Z s, V s⟫) (idxAlong γ V Z s) s` at every `s`, from *germ-level* chart data —
  which is available at every `s` from `IsJacobiAt cov γ J s` + `covAlong_eq_chart`;
* the integrand is **continuous** on `[0,t]` (each point has a neighbourhood on which the chart formula
  is continuous, and `idxAlong`/`bilAlong` are given by that formula — a purely local-to-global
  argument, no cover);
* hence the FTC (`Commons.Analysis.Calculus.integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt_of_continuousOn_Icc`,
  requested from the fleet this session) applies, and
  `∫_0^t idxAlong = ⟪∇J t, J t⟫ - ⟪∇J 0, J 0⟫ = 0`,
  `∫_0^t bilAlong = ⟪∇J t, W t⟫ - ⟪∇J 0, W 0⟫ = ⟪∇J t, W t⟫` (as `W 0 = 0`).

The **energy side** still needs the per-piece chart data (`SecondVarGlobal.energy_second_deriv_piece`
per piece of a cover of `[0,L]`, with `t` a partition point), because the second variation of the
energy is only available chart-wise.  But here the smoothness problem **dissolves**: the fields
`J + εW` (left of `t`) and `εW` (right of `t`) are smooth along `γ` *everywhere*, so the per-piece
coordinate function can be taken to be

* `chartCoords z_k γ J + ε • (χ • c)`-coordinates on pieces with `c_{k+1} ≤ t`,
* `ε • …` on pieces with `t ≤ c_k`,

without any junction condition, and the *rooms* may straddle `t` freely (`energy_second_deriv_piece`
has **no endpoint hypotheses** on the field).

