### 102.4 GOTCHAS OF THIS SESSION (they cost real time)
* **`lake env lean F.lean` does not rebuild `F`'s `.olean`.**  A *stale* `Submission/JacobiCover.olean`
  silently made `IndexFTC` see the OLD signature of `exists_partition_jacobiCoords`, and the error
  messages ("the expected type is `∀ t ∈ Ioo (E k) (A k), …`") were complete nonsense.  **Always**
  `lake build Submission.<F>` after editing `F` before elaborating a dependent file.
* **`Set.Subset` is `∀ ⦃a⦄, a ∈ s → a ∈ t` with the element *implicit*.**  If `h : s ⊆ t` then `h hx`
  (one argument) is the application, and writing `h x hx` makes Lean try `x` as the *proof* → error
  "The argument `x` has type `T` but is expected to have type `?m ∈ s`".  (This produced a dozen
  spurious errors before it was spotted.)
* **`simp only` sometimes does not fire on a hypothesis `h : u r = chartCoord x₀ γ r`** while it fires
  on the analogous `h : w r = deriv (chartCoord x₀ γ) r`, reporting the argument as *unused* (the
  unused-simp-argument linter is the tell-tale).  Workaround: `simp only [chartCovDeriv]` (unfold)
  followed by explicit `rw` — which works.
* **`obtain` with a flat pattern of 12 names on a right-nested 12-fold conjunction inside an
  existential worked only after splitting into `obtain ⟨…, hrest⟩` + explicit projections** in one
  case; when it misbehaves, use explicit projections `hrest.1`, `hrest.2.1`, … — they are also the
  most informative form (each error names the conjunct).
* `mem_nhds_iff.mp` is **ambiguous** (root vs `Metric`): write `Metric.mem_nhds_iff.mp`
  (`∃ ε > 0, ball x ε ⊆ s`) or `mem_nhds_iff.mp` after opening the right namespace.
* `isOpen_inter` does **not** exist: use `h₁.inter h₂ : IsOpen (s ∩ t)`.
* `(hUopen.inter isOpen_ball).mem_nhds ⟨…⟩` mis-elaborates (dot notation pre-applies the argument);
  write `IsOpen.mem_nhds (hUopen.inter isOpen_ball) ⟨…⟩`.
* `ContDiffOn.contDiffAt h hs` and `ContDiffAt.contDiffWithinAt` are the two bridges needed to turn a
  *pointwise* `ContDiffAt` statement into `ContDiffOn` (which is defined pointwise) — no compactness
  lemma is needed.
* The `IsJacobiPiece` / `IsBilPiece` conjunctions have **14 / 15 conjuncts** respectively; count them
  (`#print` the def) before writing the `⟨…⟩` pattern — an extra `?_` is reported as
