### 103.7 THE ONE REMAINING TECHNICAL HURDLE FOUND WHILE PLANNING §103.6 (important)

The computation `E''(0)/2 = ∫_0^t idxAlong γ V₁ ∇V₁ + ∫_t^L idxAlong γ V₂ ∇V₂` (with
`V₁ = J + εW`, `V₂ = εW`) needs the **polarisation expansion under the integral**:
`idxAlong γ (A + δB) (C + δD) = idxAlong γ A C + 2δ·bilAlong γ A B C D + δ²·idxAlong γ B D`
(`IndexFTC.idxAlong_add_smul`, a *pointwise* identity).  Turning the pointwise identity into the
identity of integrals

`∫_0^t idxAlong γ V₁ ∇V₁ = ∫_0^t idxAlong γ J ∇J + 2ε ∫_0^t bilAlong γ J W (∇J)(∇W) + ε² ∫_0^t idxAlong γ W ∇W`

uses `intervalIntegral.integral_add`, whose hypothesis is **`IntervalIntegrable` of each summand**.
(Note `∫ f = 0` does *not* give `IntervalIntegrable f`: the Bochner integral of a non-integrable
function is 0 by convention.)  So the missing library fact is

> **`IntervalIntegrable (fun t => idxAlong γ V (covAlong cov V) t) volume a b`**
> for `γ` a smooth unit-speed geodesic and `V` smooth along `γ`.

Two ways to get it:
1. **The cover route** — `SmoothFieldCover.exists_partition_smoothField` +
   `EnergyRayCover.intervalIntegrable_piece_idxAlong` per piece +
   `IntervalIntegrable.trans` (additivity over adjacent intervals) via a `Finset` induction.
   (~70 lines.)  `bilAlong`-integrability then follows from the pointwise polarisation
   `IndexIntrinsic2.bilAlong_polar` and `IntervalIntegrable.sub/add`, **which needs
   `covAlong cov (V+W) = covAlong cov V + covAlong cov W` pointwise** — a new lemma
   `covAlong_add` (hypotheses `SmoothAlongAt γ V t`, `SmoothAlongAt γ W t`, so that
   `chartCoords z γ (V+W) = chartCoords z γ V + chartCoords z γ W` and `deriv` distributes).
2. **The continuity route** — `intervalIntegral` of a continuous function on `[a,b]` is
   interval-integrable (`ContinuousOn.intervalIntegrable`), so it suffices to prove
   `ContinuousOn (fun t => idxAlong γ V (covAlong cov V) t) (Icc a b)`; this is the same cover
   argument with `IndexIntrinsic2.continuousOn_idxAlong_weak` in place of the integrability lemma.

**Also needed for §103.6 (small lemmas, listed for the next session):**
* `covAlong_add` (above), and `SmoothAlongAt γ Z s` for `Z := covAlong cov J` if one wants the
