## 114. THE PARALLEL FIELD ALONG A GEODESIC IS GLOBALLY SMOOTH AND PARALLEL (items 1 of §113.3bis)

### 114.1 What was built: `Submission/ParallelRoom.lean`

`Submission/ParallelGlobal` (session 19) glues the chart-level solutions of `y' = -Γ̂ y` into the
global parallel field `parallelField` along a geodesic.  Its weakness, recorded in §113.1, was that
the *values* of `exists_parallelChart`'s solution are only controlled on the closed piece, so the
field's smoothness (and hence `covAlong`, which is defined through the chart coordinates) was
unavailable **at the junctions of the cover**.  `Submission/ParallelRoom.lean` (namespace
`Submission.ParallelRoom`, imported by `Submission.lean`) fixes this by re-running the chart ODE on a
**symmetric room** around each piece, and then glueing by **uniqueness of the parallel field**.

