## §119 SESSION 21 (continued) — THE DETERMINANT OF THE COMPOSITE HOLONOMY

New module **`Submission.HolDet`** (imported, sorry-free, axiom-clean).

### 119.1 CONTENTS
* `coordC z γ k` — the chart coordinate curve `t ↦ extChartAt I (z k) (γ t)`;
* **`pieceTrans htor hu hw htgt k hk`** — the chart-level parallel transport along the piece
  `[P.t k, P.t (k+1)]`, defined as `FundSol.fundSol … (P.t (k+1))` (so it is the fundamental solution
  of `y' = -Γ̂ y` in the chart `z k`, evaluated at the right endpoint);
  **`pieceTrans_det_pos`** — its determinant is `> 0`, directly from `FundSol.fundSol_det_pos`;
* **`holAux htor hu hw htgt : ℕ → E →L[ℝ] E`** — the composite holonomy in the chart `z 0` at the
  base point, by structural recursion:
  `holAux (k+1) = (τ_k * Φ_k) * holAux k` for `k < P.N` (and `holAux (k+1) = holAux k` otherwise),
  where `τ_k = chartTransition (z k) (z (k+1)) (γ (P.t (k+1)))` and `Φ_k = pieceTrans … k`.
  The multiplication is the monoid of `E →L[ℝ] E` (`(f * g) x = f (g x)`), so `holAux P.N` is
  `τ_{N-1} ∘ Φ_{N-1} ∘ ⋯ ∘ τ_0 ∘ Φ_0` — the application order is `Φ_0` first;
* `factor htor hu hw htgt k` — the determinant factor `det (τ_k) · det (Φ_k)` of the piece `k`, and
  `1` outside `[0, P.N)` (a `dite`, so that it is a *total* function — this is what makes the
  induction and `Finset.prod` manipulations work);
* **`det_holAux`** — `LinearMap.det (holAux n) = ∏ k < n, factor k`, by induction, using
  `det_toLinearMap_mul` (`det ((f * g).toLinearMap) = det f · det g`, from `LinearMap.det_comp`);
* `sign_prod` — `(if 0 < ∏ f then 1 else -1) = ∏ (if 0 < f i then 1 else -1)` for a finite product
  of nonzero reals (induction + `Submission.OrientSign.ite_pos_mul_ite`);
* **`sign_det_holAux`** — **`(if 0 < det (holAux P.N) then 1 else -1) = loopSignOf P γ z`**;
* **`sign_det_holAux_eq_one_of_loopSignOf_eq_one`** — the same with `loopSignOf = 1`, i.e. **the
  composite holonomy of a null-homotopic chart-covered loop is orientation preserving**.

### 119.2 WHAT THIS IS, AND WHAT IS LEFT
`sign_det_holAux` is the determinant identity of Roadmap §115.2 in its analytic form: the chart-level
part contributes a *positive* factor (`FundSol.fundSol_det_pos`) and the chart transitions contribute
exactly `chartSign` — by *definition* of `chartDet`/`chartSign` as the determinant/sign of
`chartTransition`, which is what `Submission.OrientSign` uses.  With
`exists_chartLoop_of_simplyConnected` this proves **the sign half of `det P = 1`** for the composite
holonomy `holAux`.

What is left for the Synge input (Roadmap §118):
1. identify `holAux` with the *intrinsic* parallel transport: it must be an isometry of the fibre at
   `p` (`Hol` preserves `chartGram (z 0) p`) and it must fix the coordinate of the velocity field.
   The chart-level ingredients are the metric-compatibility of the chart parallel equation and
   `w_k := deriv (coordC … k)` solving it (`Submission.ParallelGlobal.pieceSol_deriv`-style);
2. a fixed vector in the orthogonal complement of the velocity
   (`Commons.LinearAlgebra.Orthogonal.fixed_vector_compl_of_det_one`), i.e. a **periodic parallel
   normal field** along the closed geodesic;
3. the second variation along it (`Submission.IndexLemma`, `Submission.SecondVar2`) and the
   shortening, i.e. Synge's lemma and the even-dimensional case of Klingenberg's estimate.

### 119.3 GOTCHAS OF THIS STEP
* **`Finset.prod` requires a `CommMonoid`**, so a product of *non-commuting* continuous linear maps
  cannot use it: use a structural recursion on `ℕ` (as in `holAux`) — the determinant does not care
  about the order, but the isometry/velocity statements of step 1 do, and the recursion above gets the
  application order right.
* **`MonoidHom.map_prod`/`map_prod` require a `CommMonoid` on the source**, so the multiplicativity
  of `LinearMap.det` over a product of *non-commuting* maps must be proved by hand:
  `det_toLinearMap_mul : LinearMap.det ((f * g).toLinearMap) = LinearMap.det f.toLinearMap * LinearMap.det g.toLinearMap`,
  with the bridge `(f * g).toLinearMap = f.toLinearMap.comp g.toLinearMap` proved by `ext v; rfl`.
* A `dite` **inside a `Finset.prod` binder** cannot be rewritten by `dif_pos` before the product is
  split: apply `Finset.prod_range_succ` first, then `dif_pos`/`dif_neg` on the split-off factor.
* A product `X * 1` needs `mul_one`, not `one_mul`.
* Hypotheses of a recursive `def` (here `hu hw htgt`) are *explicit arguments* and must be passed in
  every recursive call (`holAux htor hu hw htgt k`), otherwise Lean unifies the first argument with
  `k`.
* `rw [ih]` can only fire once the `dite` around `holAux m` has been eliminated by `dif_pos`/`dif_neg`.
* In `Submission.OrientSign` the structure is `Submission.OrientSign.Partition` (there is another
  `Partition` in Mathlib): `open Submission.OrientSign` (or qualify) in files using it.

## §120 SESSION 21 (continued) — THE CHART VELOCITY IS PARALLEL

`Submission.HolDet.fundSol_velocity` (added in §4 of the module): on a piece of a chart cover of a
**geodesic**, the chart velocity `deriv (coordC z γ k)` is a solution of the parallel equation
`y' = -Γ̂ y`, hence the chart transport along the piece **fixes** it:

> `pieceTrans … k hk (deriv (coordC z γ k) (P.t k)) = deriv (coordC z γ k) (P.t (k+1))`.

Proof: `Submission.ParallelGlobal.chartGeodesicVectorField_eq_neg_gammaOp` converts the chart geodesic
equation (a hypothesis `hgeo`, available in the application from
`Submission.GeodesicChart.chartGeodesicVectorField_eq_of_isGeodesicAt`) into the parallel equation for
the velocity, and `FundSol.fundSol_eqOn` (uniqueness for the vector parallel equation) identifies the
transported datum with the velocity at the right endpoint.

This is the first of the two remaining ingredients for the Synge input (Roadmap §119.2 item 1); what
still needs the *frame-change* formula is the compatibility of the velocity with the chart transitions
`τ_k` (so that `holAux` fixes the velocity coordinate), and what still needs the metric-compatibility
of the chart parallel equation is the **isometry** statement (`holAux` preserves `chartGram (z 0) p`).

## §121 SESSION 22 — THE SYNGE INPUT OF THE EVEN-DIMENSIONAL KLINGENBERG ESTIMATE IS PROVED

New module **`Submission.HolSynge`** (imported by `Submission.lean` after `Submission.HolDet`,
sorry-free, axiom-clean).  This closes ***both*** remaining ingredients of Roadmap §119.2 item 1 (the
identification of the composite holonomy with a metric object) and adds Synge's linear-algebra input:

> **`Submission.HolDet.exists_fixed_normal_coord`** — let `γ` be a **closed** chart-covered curve with
> `IsChartLoop P γ z`, whose chart velocity is a solution of the chart geodesic equation, whose chart
> Gram form is that of a metric, whose chart velocity is periodic
> (`deriv (coordC P.N) (P.t P.N) = deriv (coordC 0) (P.t 0)`), nonzero, and whose loop sign is `1`.
> If `Module.finrank ℝ E` is **even**, then there is `v ≠ 0` in the coordinates of the chart `z 0`
> with
> `chartGram (z 0) (γ (P.t 0)) (deriv (coordC 0) (P.t 0)) v = 0` (**normal to the velocity**) and
> `holAux … P.N v = v` (**fixed by the composite holonomy**).

This is *exactly* the Synge input: applied to a closed geodesic of a compact simply connected
even-dimensional manifold (with `(P, z)` from
`Submission.OrientSign.exists_chartLoop_of_simplyConnected`, whose `loopSignOf` is `1` by §118), it
produces the periodic parallel *normal* field along the closed geodesic; the second variation along
that field then shortens the geodesic (a separate step).

### 121.1 THE CONTENTS OF `Submission/HolSynge` (all `Submission.HolDet.<name>`)

| name | statement |
| --- | --- |
| `chartGram_holAux_loop` | for a closed chart loop (`γ (P.t P.N) = γ (P.t 0)`), `holAux P.N` **preserves the chart Gram form** at the base point: `chartGram (z 0) p (A v) (A w) = chartGram (z 0) p v w` |
| `det_holAux_pos` | `0 < det (holAux P.N)` from `loopSignOf P γ z = 1` (`sign_det_holAux` + `if_pos` case analysis) |
| `clmC`, `frameC`, `frameC_apply`, `clmC_apply` | the chart trivialisation `clmC z q : TangentSpace I q →ₗ E` and its inverse `frameC z q : E →ₗ TangentSpace I q`, as **linear maps** |
| `frameVector_inj` | `frameVector z q` is injective on the chart source |
| `frameEquiv`, `frameEquiv_apply`, `frameEquiv_symm_apply` | `frameC`/`clmC` packaged as a `LinearEquiv E ≃ₗ[ℝ] TangentSpace I q` |
| `intrHol` | the **intrinsic composite holonomy** `frameC ∘ₗ holAux P.N ∘ₗ clmC`, an endomorphism of `TangentSpace I (γ (P.t 0))` |
| `intrHol_apply`, `intrHol_det` | `intrHol v = frameVector … (holAux P.N (clmC v))`; `det (intrHol) = det (holAux P.N)` (a `LinearMap.det_conj`) |
| `intrHol_inner` | **`intrHol` is an isometry**: `⟪intrHol x, intrHol y⟫ = ⟪x, y⟫` (from `chartGram_holAux_loop` + `chartGram_apply`) |
