### 121.2 THE ONE IMPORT-SAFETY PROBLEM OF THE COMMONS (IMPORTANT — READ BEFORE IMPORTING)
`Submission/Commons/LinearAlgebra/Orthogonal/det_sq_eq_one_of_inner_preserving.lean` **re-declares**
`Commons.LinearAlgebra.Orthogonal.det_adjoint_eq_det` (it is already declared in
`.../odd_dim_det_one_fixed_vector.lean`).  Consequently **importing both files is a hard error**
("environment already contains 'Commons.LinearAlgebra.Orthogonal.det_adjoint_eq_det'") — and most of
the project transitively imports `odd_dim_det_one_fixed_vector`.  Do **not** import
`det_sq_eq_one_of_inner_preserving`; use the import-safe
`Commons.LinearAlgebra.Orthogonal.det_eq_one_of_inner_preserving_of_pos` instead (it imports
`odd_dim_det_one_fixed_vector` and re-proves the square identity locally).  Fixing the broken file
requires an edit inside `Submission/Commons` (not writable by a workspace agent).

### 121.3 WHAT IS STILL MISSING FOR THE INSTANTIATION OF `exists_fixed_normal_coord`

The hypotheses of `exists_fixed_normal_coord` are of two kinds:
* **combinatorial/chart**: `IsChartLoop P γ z` (given, with `loopSignOf = 1`, by
  `exists_chartLoop_of_simplyConnected`), and `hsrc`, `hu`, `hw`, `htgt`, `hdiff` (consequences of
  `IsChartLoop` + smoothness of `γ`);
* **geodesic**: `hgeo` (the chart geodesic equation on each closed piece `Icc (P.t k) (P.t (k+1))`)
  and the periodic/nonvanishing chart velocity.
`hgeo` on the *closed* piece is **not** an immediate consequence of "$γ$ is a geodesic": at the
junctions the chart `z k` need not cover a neighbourhood.  It is, however, *derivable*: by
`IsChartLoop` (which gives `γ x ∈ source (z k)` at **both** endpoints of the piece) plus openness of
the chart source plus continuity of `γ`, the chart `z k` covers a **room** `Ioo (A k) (B k)` with
`A k < P.t k` and `P.t (k+1) < B k`; on that room the chart geodesic equation is
`Submission.GeodesicGlobal.chartODE_of_isGeodesic` (or
`Submission.GeodesicChart.chartGeodesicVectorField_eq_of_isGeodesicAt`), whence on the closed piece by
restriction.  The two tools needed are:
* **`Commons.Topology.Order.exists_pos_forall_Icc_mem_of_continuousOn_isOpen`** (requested this
  session): `s` open, `f` continuous on `Icc A B`, `f '' Icc a b ⊆ s` ⟹ some `δ > 0` with
  `f '' Icc (a-δ) (b+δ) ⊆ s` and `δ ≤ min (a-A) (B-b)` — the room exists;
* the globally smooth section `Z` of the velocity along `γ`
  (`Submission.CurveField.exists_contMDiff_section_eventuallyEq_curveVelocity`), which is what
  `chartODE_of_isGeodesic` needs.

Then the remaining steps of the even-dimensional case are the **second variation along the periodic
parallel normal field** (shortening; the machinery is `Submission.IndexLemma`/`SecondVar2`/`Synge`-
style) and the **lifting argument** (Roadmap §113.2, whose correct form is the homotopy lifting for
`exp : TM → M` plus Rauch I).

### 121.4 GOTCHAS OF THIS SESSION
* **`fixed_vector_compl_of_det_one` (and any commons lemma with an implicit `{e}`):** if `e` is only
  inferred from the expected type of a *tactic block* argument, `intro h0` inside that block gets
  `h0 : ?e = 0` with `?e` a **metavariable**, and every later `rw [h0]` fails with the unhelpful
  "the pattern to be substituted is a metavariable".  Pass `(e := …)` explicitly (or use named
  arguments for all of `hf hfdim he hfe hdet`).
* `rw [clm_frameVector (I := I) hqs]` **fails** ("the pattern to be substituted is a metavariable"):
  the implicit `w` of that lemma is not inferred by `rw`'s matcher.  Supply it:
  `rw [clm_frameVector (I := I) hqs w]`.
* `FiniteDimensional ℝ (TangentSpace I x)` is **not** found by instance search: add
  `haveI : FiniteDimensional ℝ (TangentSpace I x) := inferInstanceAs (FiniteDimensional ℝ E)` before
  using `Even (Module.finrank ℝ (TangentSpace I x))` or the fixed-vector lemma.
* `LinearEquiv.ofLinear f g h1 h2` wants `h1 : f ∘ₗ g = 1` **first** (not `g ∘ g = 1`); the error
  message shows the goal, so read it.  (`ofLinear` is deprecated in favour of `ofLinearMap` but
  works.)
* The composite holonomy of a **general** closed chart-covered curve does **not** fix the velocity
  coordinate: at `k = P.N` the induction produces `clm (z P.N) (γ (P.t P.N)) (curveVelocity γ (P.t P.N))`
  and one needs `curveVelocity γ 1 = curveVelocity γ 0`, which is **not** implied by `γ 1 = γ 0`.
  The right formulation is therefore in terms of the *chart* velocity `deriv (coordC k) (P.t k)` and
  the hypothesis `deriv (coordC P.N) (P.t P.N) = deriv (coordC 0) (P.t 0)` (a `C¹` *periodic* curve,
  i.e. a map `S¹ → M`); for a genuine closed geodesic this is automatic.

