  families (`C`-derived vs. the user's `hu hw htgt`) are *different terms of the same `Prop` type*, so
  they must be identified by `Subsingleton.elim` before `holAuxC` can be identified with `holAux`
  (`rw [Subsingleton.elim …]`, as in `exists_fixed_normal_coord_of_isChartLoop`).  This is the only
  bookkeeping left; there is **no mathematics** left in the identification.
* Do **not** try to state the identification with `holAux` directly and a generic cover: `holAux`'s
  `P, z` are *section variables*, so `C.N → P.N` cannot be rewritten in it.  `holAuxC` (explicit
  arguments) is what makes the rewriting possible; that is the whole reason it exists.
* `transport C htor hN v` lives in `TangentSpace I (γ (C.c C.N))` and `holAux … P.N v` in
